          "review": [{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jatin Varma"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The luxury features like ventilated and powered front seats, panoramic sunroof, and 10-speaker JBL audio with Dolby Atmos create a premium cabin experience that easily rivals European SUVs.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.9,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Divya Pillai"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"Tata offering a lifetime battery warranty (for the first buyer) is a massive confidence booster. It eliminates the biggest financial risk of owning an EV and shows faith in their LFP battery technology.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3.7,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Anil Sastry"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"I chose the smaller 65 kWh battery variant. The 538 km claimed range is perfect for my 90% city driving, and it saved me a significant amount upfront. Great option for those who don't need the AWD.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.4,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ritu Aggarwal"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The sheer torque of 504 Nm and instant power delivery is intoxicating. Driving this car in 'Boost Mode' is an adrenaline rush I didn't expect from a Tata SUV. It transforms the Harrier's character.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":5,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sunil Das"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The smart features like Summon Mode and Auto-Park Assist are great gimmicks, but they work flawlessly. It's a fun way to show off the technology, though I rarely use them in day-to-day driving.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.8,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Amitabh Gupte"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The price, starting at ₹21.49 Lakh, is highly disruptive for an EV with this range and tech. Tata has priced it aggressively to ensure it maintains its market lead. Excellent value for a flagship EV SUV.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.9,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Kavita Rao"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"While the exterior is familiar, the grey-and-white interior theme and the twin digital displays look incredibly modern. It has a high-tech cabin that justifies the premium price tag.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Nitin Nair"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The Vehicle-to-Load (V2L) and V2V charging capabilities are game-changers. I can power my entire camping setup or even help a stranded EV friend. True utility in an emergency.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3.8,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Vijay Patel"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The 120 kW DC fast charging is excellent (20-80% in 25 minutes). This is what makes a massive 75 kWh battery practical for long journeys. You stop for coffee, the car charges quickly.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3.9,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Shreya Joshi"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The biggest downside is the stiff seating comfort. The raised floor to accommodate the battery affects under-thigh support, making the seats less comfortable on very long drives than the diesel Harrier.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Deepak Varma"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"Tata has finally delivered a true off-roader EV. The Quad Wheel Drive (QWD) with dedicated terrain modes (Rock Crawl, Sand) gives me confidence to take it to rough terrains where no other EV dares to go.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.1,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gaurav Kulkarni"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The 14.5-inch Samsung Neo QLED touchscreen is a futuristic centerpiece. The clarity is amazing, and integrating the 540° Surround View with Transparent View is invaluable for navigating tight city parking and off-roading.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3.8,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Dr. Ananya Singh"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The safety features are top-notch. A 5-star BNCAP rating combined with Level 2 ADAS (Adaptive Cruise Control, Lane Keep Assist, etc.) makes it one of the safest cars on Indian roads. A genuine family protector.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4.3,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Pooja Tandon"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"The 627 km claimed range is fantastic for highway trips, and the real-world range of over 450 km is highly dependable. Range anxiety is officially dead, especially when backed by Tata's fast-charging network.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":4,"bestRating":"5"}},{"@type":"Review","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Rajiv Menon"},"datePublished":"2025-10-25","reviewBody":"A truly game-changing EV. I went for the Empowered QWD 75 kWh variant, and the 390 bhp AWD performance is breathtaking. 0-100 km/h in 6.3 seconds in an SUV this size is simply phenomenal.","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":3.9,"bestRating":"5"}}]

